Here's a JavaScript implementation for packing and unpacking an array of entities into an ArrayBuffer. The entities have the fields `id` (4 bits) and `size` (3 bits).

```javascript
function packEntities(entities) {
  const buffer = new ArrayBuffer(entities.length);
  const view = new DataView(buffer);

  for (let i = 0; i < entities.length; i++) {
    const entity = entities[i];
    const id = entity.id & 0xF; // Masking to get the lower 4 bits
    const size = entity.size & 0x7; // Masking to get the lower 3 bits

    // Write the id and size to the buffer
    view.setUint16(i * (id + size), id | (size << 3), true);

    // Write the entity data starting from the next byte
    const offset = (i * (id + size)) + 2;
    const dataLength = entity.data.length;
    if (dataLength > view.byteLength - offset) {
      throw new Error("Entity data too large for buffer");
    }
    view.set(new Uint8Array(entity.data), offset);
  }

  return buffer;
}

function unpackEntities(buffer, count) {
  const view = new DataView(buffer);
  const entities = [];

  for (let i = 0; i < count; i++) {
    const id = view.getUint16(i * (view.getUint16(i) >> 3), true) >> 3;
    const size = view.getUint16(i * (view.getUint16(i) >> 3), true) & 0x7;
    const dataLength = size === 0 ? 0 : view.byteLength - (i * (id + size + 2));
    const data = new Uint8Array(buffer, i * (id + size + 2), dataLength);

    entities.push({
      id: id,
      size: size,
      data: data
    });
  }

  return entities;
}
```

In the `packEntities` function, we create an ArrayBuffer and a DataView to manipulate the buffer. We iterate through the entities and pack each one into the buffer. The id and size are written as a 16-bit unsigned integer, with the id in the lower 4 bits and the size in the upper 3 bits. The entity data is written starting from the next byte after the id and size.

In the `unpackEntities` function, we create an ArrayView and iterate through the buffer to unpack the entities. We calculate the id and size from the first 16-bit unsigned integer at each position, and then determine the length of the data based on the id and size. The data is extracted as a new Uint8Array from the buffer. The unpacked entities are returned as an array.

